{
  "version": 1,
  "sections": {
    "vlm": [
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "children": [
          {
            "text": "But it hasn't necessarily learned the detailed relationship between those observations and a robot's 50-step motor trajectory."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "context": [
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "children": [
          {
            "text": "This is the entire ingestion engine (fancy fancy words). "
          },
          {
            "tag": "br",
            "children": []
          },
          {
            "text": "During training, provides all the context needed to predict the future 50 actions the robot needs to take:"
          },
          {
            "tag": "br",
            "children": []
          },
          {
            "tag": "ul",
            "children": [
              {
                "tag": "li",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Full images from 3 (or 4) cameras;"
                  },
                  {
                    "tag": "br",
                    "children": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "tag": "li",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Text, which includes instructions & metadata;"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "tag": "li",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Proprioception, which tells the robot where IT is;"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "tag": "li",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Visual subgoals, provided "
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "by the BAGEL world model (ehhh);"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "observation": [
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "children": [
          {
            "text": "This follow a standard VLM encoder architecture. "
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "children": [
          {
            "text": "Images are captured in batches of 6 frames, patchified, infused with positional and temporal embeddings "
          },
          {
            "tag": "u",
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "(counterintuitive, yes, like why would you even patchify in the first place? lol)."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "tag": "br",
            "children": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "children": [
          {
            "text": "They go through 27 transformer layers, with spatial and temporal attention. The shape of the output remains [B, V, 6, 1024, 1152], where information has been shared among the V * 6 * 1024 patches of every batch. "
          },
          {
            "tag": "strong",
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "The concept of \"frame\" is lost at this point."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "children": [
          {
            "text": "To match dimensions downstream, the tensor is reduced to "
          },
          {
            "tag": "br",
            "children": []
          },
          {
            "text": "[B, V, "
          },
          {
            "tag": "strong",
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "(1), "
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "1024, 1152]."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "children": [
          {
            "text": " "
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "observation-input": [
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "children": [
          {
            "text": "Hopefully, straightforward enough - it's a little video. "
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "patches": [
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "children": [
          {
            "text": "With patch size 14 x 14, there are 1024 patches per image channel."
          },
          {
            "tag": "br",
            "children": []
          },
          {
            "text": "With 3 channels (RGB), each patch is effectively a 14 x 14 x 3 prism."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "children": [
          {
            "text": "We flatten out the 14 x 14 x 3 = 588 values, project to 1152 through "
          },
          {
            "tag": "strong",
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Linear(588, 1152), "
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "and now call what used to be patches \"tokens\". "
          },
          {
            "text": " "
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "embeddings": [
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "children": [
          {
            "text": "One of the weirder steps in a standard VLM encoder, where, at the cost of parallelism, position in the original video is completely lost. "
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "children": [
          {
            "text": "For a video, it's trivial to recognize where each patch belongs both in "
          },
          {
            "tag": "strong",
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "space and time"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": ", but, flattened, we need to reintroduce them to the tensor. "
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "children": [
          {
            "tag": "u",
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Time and space embeddings can be fixed or learned parameters. "
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "vision-backbone": [
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "children": [
          {
            "text": "27 layers of vanilla spatial attention, where every token can attend to every other token on the same frame. "
          },
          {
            "tag": "br",
            "children": []
          },
          {
            "text": "Every 4 classical blocks, there is one temporal layer. "
          },
          {
            "tag": "br",
            "children": []
          },
          {
            "text": "Pure multi-headed attention, with 1:1 Q/K ratios. "
          },
          {
            "tag": "br",
            "children": []
          },
          {
            "text": "It is "
          },
          {
            "tag": "strong",
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "okay"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": " to view all transformer blocks in this paper as black boxes."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
